<h1>Flim Summaries</h1>
<p class="lede-inline">
  Flim can create voice-message titles, summaries, and transcripts in several
  ways. Flim Summaries is one of those ways, provided by Flim itself.
</p>

<p>
  In Flim's settings, you choose which service to use for voice message titles, summaries, and transcripts.
  You can choose between:
  <ul>
    <li>Flim Summaries (this service, run by the same people who create Flim)</li>
    <li>An external service of your choice (e.g. OpenAI, Google, etc.)</li>
    <li>Your own on-device AI (if your phone supports it)</li>
  </ul>
  If you select Flim Summaries as the service, Flim sends the voice message and a
  little chat context from previous messages in the chat to this service. What Flim Summaries does is:
  <ul>
    <li>Runs speech-to-text on the voice message</li>
    <li>Creates a title and a summary of the transcript, using a small AI model</li>
  </ul>
  All of the speech-to-text and summarisation is done within the EU by service providers that do not
  store any of the data, and do not use the data to train their models. See Privacy Policy for the list of providers that Flim Summaries uses.
 </p>


